@@@!atrep-exo
@=litogramma=>gemtext

@@/ Gemtext export: the maximal-loss surface. Three heading
@@/ levels (deeper levels cap at ###), no inline formatting
@@/ (everything dissolves to plain text), links as their bare
@@/ URL in the running text (the => link line is a line form,
@@/ invalid mid-paragraph), verse and tables as preformatted
@@/ lines, notes
@@/ inlined as bracketed asides after their paragraphs. The
@@/ motivating specimen for loss-graded routing: compare this
@@/ path's losses with the HTML path's.

